    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i have a 2018 honda civic and every time i hit the gas there is this really loud squealing noise coming from under the hood. can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a long, ribbed belt that wraps around various pulleys under your hood to drive accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor. When this belt wears down, loosens, or a pulley it's connected to develops excessive slack, it can create a loud squealing noise, especially when the engine demands more power by hitting the gas. This indicates the belt itself or one of its corresponding components likely needs inspection and replacement soon.",
      "source": "target",
