    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. does the noise mean a pulley is actually broken or is it just the belt slipping? i'm trying to figure out if i need a whole new part or just a new belt.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The noise could be caused by either, so it's difficult to tell for sure without an inspection. A slipping belt usually squeals loudly when under load, which often means the belt itself is glazed or worn out. However, a bad pulley bearing, even if the belt isn't slipping, can grind or squeal due to internal friction. A mechanic can check belt tension and bearing condition to determine precisely which part requires replacement.",
      "source": "target",
